# https://github.com/vercel/next.js/tree/canary/examples/cms-contentful
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) for `next dev`. The space id and its
# Content Delivery API token are read at BUILD time and inlined into the
# server bundle (next.config.ts): a deployed build takes them from its
# environment's CONTENTFUL_SPACE_ID and CONTENTFUL_ACCESS_TOKEN Orun secrets
# (README → Connecting Contentful). Unset, the blog is unconnected: it renders
# its bundled sample posts under a "connect your Contentful space" notice.
CONTENTFUL_SPACE_ID=
CONTENTFUL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Draft mode and the revalidate webhook read these at request time: here for
# `next dev`; on stage and prod they are Worker secrets (see .dev.vars.example).
CONTENTFUL_PREVIEW_ACCESS_TOKEN=
CONTENTFUL_PREVIEW_SECRET=
CONTENTFUL_REVALIDATE_SECRET=
